{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../state.json'))\nv=s['materials'];print(type(v).__name__)\nif isinstance(v,dict):\n for k in ['i_verify','s_verify','s_loop','s_notify']: print(k,json.dumps(v.get(k),indent=2)[:1800])\nelse:\n for x in v:\n  if x.get('id') in ['i_verify','s_verify','s_loop','s_notify']:print(json.dumps(x,indent=2)[:1800])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"list\n{\n  \"id\": \"s_loop\",\n  \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n  \"start_line\": 667,\n  \"end_line\": 963,\n  \"kind\": \"code_observation\",\n  \"text\": \"func (r *Raft) leaderLoop() {\\n\\t// stepDown is used to track if there is an inflight log that\\n\\t// would cause us to lose leadership (specifically a RemovePeer of\\n\\t// ourselves). If this is the case, we must not allow any logs to\\n\\t// be processed in parallel, otherwise we are basing commit on\\n\\t// only a single peer (ourself) and replicating to an undefined set\\n\\t// of peers.\\n\\tstepDown := false\\n\\t// This is only used for the first lease check, we reload lease below\\n\\t// based on the current config value.\\n\\tlease := time.After(r.config().LeaderLeaseTimeout)\\n\\n\\tfor r.getState() == Leader {\\n\\t\\tr.mainThreadSaturation.sleeping()\\n\\n\\t\\tselect {\\n\\t\\tcase rpc := <-r.rpcCh:\\n\\t\\t\\tr.mainThreadSaturation.working()\\n\\t\\t\\tr.processRPC(rpc)\\n\\n\\t\\tcase <-r.leaderState.stepDown:\\n\\t\\t\\tr.mainThreadSaturation.working()\\n\\t\\t\\tr.setState(Follower)\\n\\n\\t\\tcase future := <-r.leadershipTransferCh:\\n\\t\\t\\tr.mainThreadSaturation.working()\\n\\t\\t\\tif r.getLeadershipTransferInProgress() {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tr.logger.Debug(ErrLeadershipTransferInProgress.Error())\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tfuture.respond(ErrLeadershipTransferInProgress)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tr.logger.Debug(\\\"starting leadership transfer\\\", \\\"id\\\", future.ID, \\\"address\\\", future.Address)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// When we are leaving leaderLoop, we are no longer\\n\\t\\t\\t// leader, so we should stop transferring.\\n\\t\\t\\tleftLeaderLoop := make(chan struct{})\\n\\t\\t\\tdefer func() { close(leftLeaderLoop) }()\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tstopCh := make(chan struct{})\\n\\t\\t\\tdoneCh := make(chan error, 1)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// This is intentionally being setup outside of the\\n\\t\\t\\t// leadershipTransfer function. Because the TimeoutNow\\n\\t\\t\\t// call is bl\n{\n  \"id\": \"s_notify\",\n  \"file\": \"replication.go\",\n  \"start_line\": 31,\n  \"end_line\": 119,\n  \"kind\": \"code_observation\",\n  \"text\": \"// followerReplication is in charge of sending snapshots and log entries from\\n// this leader during this particular term to a remote follower.\\ntype followerReplication struct {\\n\\t// currentTerm and nextIndex must be kept at the top of the struct so\\n\\t// they're 64 bit aligned which is a requirement for atomic ops on 32 bit\\n\\t// platforms.\\n\\n\\t// currentTerm is the term of this leader, to be included in AppendEntries\\n\\t// requests.\\n\\tcurrentTerm uint64\\n\\n\\t// nextIndex is the index of the next log entry to send to the follower,\\n\\t// which may fall past the end of the log.\\n\\tnextIndex uint64\\n\\n\\t// peer contains the network address and ID of the remote follower.\\n\\tpeer Server\\n\\t// peerLock protects 'peer'\\n\\tpeerLock sync.RWMutex\\n\\n\\t// commitment tracks the entries acknowledged by followers so that the\\n\\t// leader's commit index can advance. It is updated on successful\\n\\t// AppendEntries responses.\\n\\tcommitment *commitment\\n\\n\\t// stopCh is notified/closed when this leader steps down or the follower is\\n\\t// removed from the cluster. In the follower removed case, it carries a log\\n\\t// index; replication should be attempted with a best effort up through that\\n\\t// index, before exiting.\\n\\tstopCh chan uint64\\n\\n\\t// triggerCh is notified every time new entries are appended to the log.\\n\\ttriggerCh chan struct{}\\n\\n\\t// triggerDeferErrorCh is used to provide a backchannel. By sending a\\n\\t// deferErr, the sender can be notified when the replication is done.\\n\\ttriggerDeferErrorCh chan *deferError\\n\\n\\t// lastContact is updated to the current time whenever any response is\\n\\t// received from the follower (successful or not). Th\n{\n  \"id\": \"s_verify\",\n  \"file\": \"raft.go\",\n  \"start_line\": 965,\n  \"end_line\": 987,\n  \"kind\": \"code_observation\",\n  \"text\": \"func (r *Raft) verifyLeader(v *verifyFuture) {\\n\\t// Current leader always votes for self\\n\\tv.votes = 1\\n\\n\\t// Set the quorum size, hot-path for single node\\n\\tv.quorumSize = r.quorumSize()\\n\\tif v.quorumSize == 1 {\\n\\t\\tv.respond(nil)\\n\\t\\treturn\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t// Track this request\\n\\tv.notifyCh = r.verifyCh\\n\\tr.leaderState.notify[v] = struct{}{}\\n\\n\\t// Trigger immediate heartbeats\\n\\tfor _, repl := range r.leaderState.replState {\\n\\t\\trepl.notifyLock.Lock()\\n\\t\\trepl.notify[v] = struct{}{}\\n\\t\\trepl.notifyLock.Unlock()\\n\\t\\tasyncNotifyCh(repl.notifyCh)\\n\\t}\\n}\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"54d43df5197fd71cd0f6ae4eee1ba28efb139a5223eb14b756c606bdb0b8a800\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"i_verify\",\n  \"file\": \"api.go\",\n  \"start_line\": 880,\n  \"end_line\": 894,\n  \"kind\": \"interface_statement\",\n  \"text\": \"// VerifyLeader is used to ensure this peer is still the leader. It may be used\\n// to prevent returning stale data from the FSM after the peer has lost\\n// leadership.\\nfunc (r *Raft) VerifyLeader() Future {\\n\\tmetrics.IncrCounter([]string{\\\"raft\\\", \\\"verify_leader\\\"}, 1)\\n\\tverifyFuture := &verifyFuture{}\\n\\tverifyFuture.init()\\n\\tselect {\\n\\tcase <-r.shutdownCh:\\n\\t\\treturn errorFuture{ErrRaftShutdown}\\n\\tcase r.verifyCh <- verifyFuture:\\n\\t\\treturn verifyFuture\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"499a72c01096912e85d16381f4640ac6d29f8c2b91cabbdae8530bdcbeb89a4a\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_obligation.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));c=r['candidates'][0];q=c['question']\nclaim_id='o_verify_superseded_authority'\nss=['i_verify','i_suffrage','i_future','s_verify','s_notify','s_future','s_loop','s_lease','s_election','s_campaign','s_commit','s_fsm']\nclaim=dict(id=claim_id,kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='With unchanged valid membership, a VerifyLeader invocation on an old leader must not complete with nil error when a different voter has already won a higher-term election and successfully applied a new command before that invocation, and the old leader has not reacquired authority during the invocation. Acknowledgements from an isolated nonvoter do not restore that superseded authority.',source_ids=ss,scope=dict(description='Public leadership-verification safety under a network partition separating the old leader and a nonvoter from the two remaining voters in a three-voter configuration. A higher-term elected leader and completed new command precede invocation on the old leader. The proposition forbids success, but permits errors or remaining pending until bounded harness shutdown.',assumptions=['Non-Byzantine actual Raft workers and transports; requests may be unavailable across a declared partition.','Static, consistently installed membership and stable participant IDs; no forced recovery, restore, or membership change during the comparison.','Observe real election and successful command application in the same execution; do not assign terms or role state.','The original leader has not rejoined or won another election before completion.'],excluded=['General liveness or deadline guarantees.','Proof of stale application reads, conflicting committed logs, crash durability, or every transport variant.','Treating absence of remote responses alone as proof of lost authority.'],parameters={'voters':3,'nonvoters':1,'required_order':'higher-term authority and applied command -> old-leader VerifyLeader invocation -> result'}),pending=['Execute the stronger same-history prefix and independently observe the result of the selected public future.','Determine whether lease timing permits the targeted overlap without suppressing protective workers.'],grounding=dict(source_ids=['s_verify','s_notify','s_future','s_loop','s_lease','s_election','s_campaign','s_commit','s_fsm'],expectation_ids=['i_verify','i_future'],binding_ids=['bind_verify_entry','bind_verify_tally'],derivation='The public VerifyLeader contract explicitly ensures the peer is still leader and allows use to prevent stale FSM reads after loss of leadership. Future.Error is its observable completion status. Rather than inventing a requirement to collect a particular number of fresh replies, this obligation establishes the antecedent of lost authority independently: another configured voter won a higher-term election and applied a new command before invocation, with no subsequent reacquisition by the old node. A nil verification result then contradicts the promised authority check regardless of the particular tally mechanism. The nonvoter path is the suspected producer of insufficient support, not the normative source of the obligation.',applicability='Ordinary online API use in a mixed-membership cluster. Network partition delays or prevents cross-partition RPCs but does not fabricate response contents, terms, votes or commits. A local role still reading Leader is precisely the stale authority condition the API must check; it cannot be assumed to validate itself.',unresolved=['A successful exploration with unchanged term and no replacement leader does not establish this antecedent.','The stronger legal prefix and public result require a new submitted check.'],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Voter-only lease check or negative/newer-term RPC may step down the old node and return error; either prevents the forbidden success.','A valid alternative authority mechanism would also satisfy the API, but local state and isolated nonvoter success cannot undo an independently observed higher-term election.','Pending verification is permitted; a finite observation deadline alone is not a violation.']))\ndef binding(i,material,symbol,a,b,description):return dict(id=i,material_id=material,symbol=symbol,start_line=a,end_line=b,description=description,pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim_id,source_ids=['i_verify','i_future'],rationale='The public authority-check contract supplies the expectation; this code binding locates admission or consumption, not an independent normative rule.')])\nq['disposition']='ready_for_check'\nq['unknowns']=['The exploration established a real elected prefix, applied command, pending verification, and nil public result after only the nonvoter response count advanced. This did not independently establish authority loss.','Execute a higher-term election and applied command on the other two voters before invoking VerifyLeader on the isolated old leader.','Observe membership, term continuity, protective lease/negative-response behavior, and the selected future result in one execution; do not infer these from local role alone.']\nsub=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=c['id'],question=q,obligation=claim,bindings=[binding('bind_verify_entry','i_verify','VerifyLeader',883,894,'Public API admits a verification future and returns its eventual status.'),binding('bind_verify_tally','s_verify','verifyLeader',965,987,'Registers the check on all replication workers with a voter-derived threshold.')],rationale='Continue the same eligibility Candidate with a requirement derived from the public authority promise, not from the observed counting difference. Exploration CheckRun e19127d466a2458fa5512e5d3e45998e completed and its events show connected success, pending isolated verification, then nil result after nonvoter successes changed from 3 to 4 while both remote voter counts stayed at 2. This answers feasibility of the local support path but not lost authority. The next discriminator establishes supersession before invocation using real workers, preserving lease and all protective paths. That is more decisive than repeating local acknowledgement counting or switching to unrelated storage faults.',feedback=dict(ref_ids=[c['id'],'e19127d466a2458fa5512e5d3e45998e'],answered='A real mixed-membership elected leader completed VerifyLeader after only its nonvoter successful-response count advanced in the partitioned exploration; the connected control also completed successfully. This is exploration, not property Evidence.',remaining=['Superseding authority must be independently produced and observed before verification invocation.','The response-count experiment does not prove exact response-consumption timing; the stronger independently established authority-loss antecedent avoids using that count as its oracle.'],understanding='unchanged',rationale='The observed local path is consistent with the existing map; no map edit is needed. Move from local eligibility feasibility to the public authority promise with a same-history supersession prefix.',question_updates={c['id']:dict(unknowns=q['unknowns'],resume_conditions=['Run a public-API check with higher-term election and applied command before old-leader verification, recording the final future result.'])}))\nimport jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(sub,json.load(open('../native-submission.schema.json')))\nPath('submission-obligation.json').write_text(json.dumps(sub,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Obligation submission passes schema validation.')\nPY\npython3 make_obligation.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
